# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. .env.local is
# gitignored — never commit actual keys.
#
# These come from the golfme-dev Supabase project (Settings > API in the
# dashboard, or `get_project_url` / `get_publishable_keys` via the Supabase
# MCP). The anon/publishable key is safe to expose client-side by design —
# access control lives in Postgres RLS, not in keeping this key secret.
# NEVER put a service_role/secret key in a VITE_ variable — Vite inlines
# every VITE_-prefixed value into the shipped frontend bundle.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Caddie's real swing analysis (supabase/functions/analyze-swing) needs a
# Gemini API key. This is a Supabase Edge Function secret ONLY — set via
# `supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=...` or the Supabase dashboard, never
# a VITE_ variable, and must never hold a real value in this file or in
# .env.local. The frontend never sees this key; it's read server-side via
# Deno.env.get("GEMINI_API_KEY") inside the Edge Function alone.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Tee-time provider credentials (Skyway/Dyker Beach) — NOT set anywhere yet.
# Neither provider has a public API; both require an approved partner-API
# relationship (Lightspeed Golf Partner API for Skyway, a Tee It Up/NBC
# Sports Next partner integration for Dyker Beach) that GolfMe doesn't have
# today. These are documented here only so the shape is ready — they are
# Supabase Edge Function secrets (`supabase secrets set`), never a VITE_
# variable, and must never hold real values in this file or in .env.local
# committed anywhere.
# LIGHTSPEED_GOLF_PARTNER_API_KEY=
# TEEITUP_PARTNER_API_KEY=
